Prerequisite fixes so the FirebaseCrashlytics example isolates the
CLS_SDK_NAME failure. Without these, the build stops earlier on unrelated
explicit-module problems in the same package.

1. The umbrella `Firebase` target's header does
   `#import <FirebaseCore/FirebaseCore.h>` but the target declares no deps, so
   `Firebase.pcm` fails with `'FirebaseCore/FirebaseCore.h' file not found`.
   Declare the dep, and drop the reverse `Firebase` edge from `FirebaseCore`
   to keep SwiftPM from seeing a cycle. That edge only re-exports the umbrella
   header; FirebaseCore's sources never import anything from `Firebase`.

2. `FirebaseCoreExtension` has the same problem via
   `#import <FirebaseCore/FIRApp.h>`. Upstream's own comment on the target
   already tells consumers to depend on `FirebaseCore` alongside it.

diff --git a/Package.swift b/Package.swift
--- a/Package.swift
+++ b/Package.swift
@@ -177,6 +177,7 @@
   targets: [
     .target(
       name: "Firebase",
+      dependencies: ["FirebaseCore"],
       path: "CoreOnly/Sources",
       publicHeadersPath: "./"
     ),
@@ -235,7 +236,6 @@
     .target(
       name: "FirebaseCore",
       dependencies: [
-        "Firebase",
         "FirebaseCoreInternal",
         .product(name: "GULEnvironment", package: "GoogleUtilities"),
         .product(name: "GULLogger", package: "GoogleUtilities"),
@@ -274,6 +274,7 @@
     // to avoid potential linker issues.
     .target(
       name: "FirebaseCoreExtension",
+      dependencies: ["FirebaseCore"],
       path: "FirebaseCore/Extension",
       resources: [.process("Resources/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy")],
       publicHeadersPath: ".",
